(a) No person may store more than 200 scrap tires anywhere in the city. Any person storing in excess of 100 scrap tires shall be deemed to be in violation of this section.
(b) Subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
(1) A solid waste disposal site permitted by the EPD if the permit authorizes the storage of scrap tires prior to their disposal;
(2) A tire retailer with not more than 2,000 scrap tires stored in a shipping container and not more than 1,000 scrap tires in storage, if such retailer complies with EPD rule 391-3-4-.19(3);
(3) A tire retreader with not more than 1,500 scrap tires in storage so long as the scrap tires are of the type the retreader is actively retreading;
(4) An auto salvage yard with not more than 500 scrap tires in storage; and
(5) A scrap tire processor approved by the EPD so long as the number of scrap tires in storage does not exceed the quantity approved by the EPD.
(c) Scrap tires illegally dumped or stored on private property shall be removed by the occupant, agent or owner of the property and transported to an end user, recycler, processor, sorter or disposal facility approved by the EPD. The person responsible for the abatement of illegally dumped or stored scrap tires shall retain copies of the manifest or receipt which shows the disposition of scrap tires.
(Ord. No. 95-27, § 4-3004, 8-24-1995)
